  "description": "Reinforcing or joining leaves and plates by pasting a narrow strip along the fold. Cockerell prefers the guard inside an outer pair to catch ragged edges and outside an inner pair to ease sewing, and he warns that stretching a pasted guard makes the sheet crinkle as it dries. Thick plates are pared at the back so the guards do not swell the spine.",
